{"schemaVersion": 1, "kind": "MESSAGE", "classes": ["org.apache.zookeeper.txn.TxnHeader"], "why": "A ZooKeeper txn's header crosses the learner stream inside a PROPOSAL's or an INFORM's data bytes (ZK_QUORUM: the tree's CausynthQuorum hands the door the header as the packet's message), so the door walks it as it walks a generated message and the zxid a learner applies pairs with the export that sent it (zk-bugs-observer-master). Jute generates the record but no CODEC row covers it: jute's runtime stays program state. A setter called on a decoded header rebinds that one field to its own export; its other fields stay decoded."}
